# PLC ↔ MQTT ↔ Node-RED | IIoT Communication

Real-time bidirectional communication between Siemens S7-1214C PLC 
and Node-RED dashboard via Mosquitto MQTT Broker.

---

## Architecture

Siemens S7-1214C → Mosquitto Broker → Node-RED
       ↑                                   |
       └───────── watchdog/value ──────────┘

---

## Topics

| Topic           | Direction        | Message        |
|-----------------|------------------|----------------|
| s71200/data     | PLC → Node-RED   | JSON string    |
| watchdog/value  | Node-RED → PLC   | Int (1..999)   |
| s71200/commands | Node-RED → PLC   | JSON string    |

---

## Software Used

| Software          | Version  |
|-------------------|----------|
| TIA Portal        | V19      |
| Mosquitto Broker  | 2.1.2    |
| Node-RED          | Latest   |

---

## Hardware Used

| Hardware              | Details              |
|-----------------------|----------------------|
| Siemens S7-1214C      | CPU 1214C DC/DC/DC   |
| Laptop / Local Server | VMware Workstation   |

---

## Setup Guide

### 1. Mosquitto Broker
- Install Mosquitto on your machine
- Replace mosquitto.conf with the one in /Mosquitto folder
- Run:
mosquitto -c mosquitto.conf -v

### 2. TIA Portal
- Import SCL files from /TIA-Portal/SCL/
- Configure LMQTT_Client FB:
  - BrokerAddress: your PC IP
  - BrokerPort: 1883
  - ClientID: PLC_1214C
- Download to PLC

### 3. Node-RED
- Import flows.json from /NodeRED/
- Install node-red-dashboard
- Configure MQTT broker node to your PC IP
- Deploy and open:
http://localhost:1880/ui

---

## PLC SCL - JSON Payload Format

### Published from PLC (s71200/data):
{"bool1":true,"bool2":false,"real1":60.0,"string1":"CURRENT"}

### Published from Node-RED (watchdog/value):
1..999 (incrementing integer)

---

## Features

- Real-time PLC data visualization on Node-RED dashboard
- Bidirectional MQTT communication
- MQTT Watchdog monitoring (connection health)
- JSON payload from PLC using SCL CONCAT
- Mosquitto broker as local server

---

## Connection Diagram

PLC (192.168.0.1) ←── Ethernet ──→ Laptop (192.168.0.100)
                                          │
                                    VMware VM
                                          │
                                  Mosquitto Broker
                                          │
                                       Node-RED

